category WalkArgouml {
    objects: CodeUnit, g0, g1, g3, m_application, m_diagrams, m_notation, m_explorer, m_codeGeneration, m_reverseEngineering, m_persistence, m_profile, m_help, m_moduleLoader, m_gui, m_model, m_internationalization, m_taskManagement, m_configuration, m_swingExtensions, m_ocl, m_critics, m_javaCodeGeneration;
    start: CodeUnit;
    admission: sealed;
    frame CodeUnit: choice "Which part of the intended architecture is responsible for this code unit?";
    frame g0: choice "Which module of this part (Low-level subsystems) is responsible for the code unit?";
    frame g1: choice "Which module of this part (View and control subsystems) is responsible for the code unit?";
    frame g3: choice "Which module of this part (Loadable subsystems) is responsible for the code unit?";
    to_g0: CodeUnit -> g0 "Low-level subsystems: infrastructure every other subsystem uses, depending on no other part of ArgoUML. Its modules: Internationalization, a low-level subsystem: the infrastructure the other subsystems use to translate strings, to plug in new languages, and to administer the default and the supported languages; TaskManagement, a low-level subsystem: everything related to the concept of task, job or request, such as monitoring the progress of a long running task; Configuration, a low-level subsystem: stores and retrieves all configurable aspects of the application, kept in the user's home directory; Swing extensions, a low-level subsystem: infrastructure for every other subsystem to use, depending on no other part of ArgoUML; Model, the Model subsystem (MVC): hides from the rest of ArgoUML which model repository is in use and gives a consistent interface for manipulating the data in it, including the important well-formedness rules";
    is_m_internationalization: g0 -> m_internationalization "Internationalization, a low-level subsystem: the infrastructure the other subsystems use to translate strings, to plug in new languages, and to administer the default and the supported languages";
    is_m_taskManagement: g0 -> m_taskManagement "TaskManagement, a low-level subsystem: everything related to the concept of task, job or request, such as monitoring the progress of a long running task";
    is_m_configuration: g0 -> m_configuration "Configuration, a low-level subsystem: stores and retrieves all configurable aspects of the application, kept in the user's home directory";
    is_m_swingExtensions: g0 -> m_swingExtensions "Swing extensions, a low-level subsystem: infrastructure for every other subsystem to use, depending on no other part of ArgoUML";
    is_m_model: g0 -> m_model "Model, the Model subsystem (MVC): hides from the rest of ArgoUML which model repository is in use and gives a consistent interface for manipulating the data in it, including the important well-formedness rules";
    to_g1: CodeUnit -> g1 "View and control subsystems: rely on the model to do their work. Its modules: Diagrams, a View subsystem: presents the diagrams to the user and lets the user manipulate them through the view; its classes extend the graph editing framework's base classes (graph models, figures, selections), and it depends on the Model and the GUI; GUI framework, a View and Control subsystem: provides an infrastructure with menus, tool bars, tabs and panes for the other subsystems to fill with actions and contents; implemented directly on top of Swing, with no knowledge of UML, critics, diagrams or the model; Explorer (formerly the Navigator), a View and Control subsystem: provides tree views of the model elements, diagrams and other objects, with configurable perspectives; Notation, a View and Control subsystem: generates, updates and edits, in different languages, the textual representation of one or more UML model elements, attached e.g. to a diagram figure or an explorer entry; Code Generation, a Control subsystem: the point where the different languages register that they can generate code, and the functions common to all languages; Reverse Engineering, a Control subsystem: a central registration point for language reverse engineering (import) modules, and the reverse engineering methods common to all languages; Module loader, a View and Control subsystem: provides the mechanisms to load and unload the auxiliary modules; modules connect and register themselves to the subsystems they work with";
    is_m_diagrams: g1 -> m_diagrams "Diagrams, a View subsystem: presents the diagrams to the user and lets the user manipulate them through the view; its classes extend the graph editing framework's base classes (graph models, figures, selections), and it depends on the Model and the GUI";
    is_m_gui: g1 -> m_gui "GUI framework, a View and Control subsystem: provides an infrastructure with menus, tool bars, tabs and panes for the other subsystems to fill with actions and contents; implemented directly on top of Swing, with no knowledge of UML, critics, diagrams or the model";
    is_m_explorer: g1 -> m_explorer "Explorer (formerly the Navigator), a View and Control subsystem: provides tree views of the model elements, diagrams and other objects, with configurable perspectives";
    is_m_notation: g1 -> m_notation "Notation, a View and Control subsystem: generates, updates and edits, in different languages, the textual representation of one or more UML model elements, attached e.g. to a diagram figure or an explorer entry";
    is_m_codeGeneration: g1 -> m_codeGeneration "Code Generation, a Control subsystem: the point where the different languages register that they can generate code, and the functions common to all languages";
    is_m_reverseEngineering: g1 -> m_reverseEngineering "Reverse Engineering, a Control subsystem: a central registration point for language reverse engineering (import) modules, and the reverse engineering methods common to all languages";
    is_m_moduleLoader: g1 -> m_moduleLoader "Module loader, a View and Control subsystem: provides the mechanisms to load and unload the auxiliary modules; modules connect and register themselves to the subsystems they work with";
    to_m_application: CodeUnit -> m_application "Application, the top level subsystem: provides the entry point when starting ArgoUML (it contains the main method) and starts the ball rolling; it initialises the other subsystems and depends on them, but no other subsystem depends on it";
    to_g3: CodeUnit -> g3 "Loadable subsystems: connected only through other subsystems' interfaces, enabled and disabled by the module loader. Its modules: Java, a loadable subsystem: converts the model into Java code and keeps it updated in Java or in the model, and converts Java code into a model (round-trip engineering for Java); Critics and other cognitive tools, a loadable subsystem: cognitive help for the user based on the current model: critics that find model elements not obeying simple design rules or best practices, checklists, wizards, and the to-do items they generate; OCL, a loadable subsystem: allows editing of strings in the OCL (Object Constraint Language), adapting an external OCL editor to ArgoUML";
    is_m_javaCodeGeneration: g3 -> m_javaCodeGeneration "Java, a loadable subsystem: converts the model into Java code and keeps it updated in Java or in the model, and converts Java code into a model (round-trip engineering for Java)";
    is_m_critics: g3 -> m_critics "Critics and other cognitive tools, a loadable subsystem: cognitive help for the user based on the current model: critics that find model elements not obeying simple design rules or best practices, checklists, wizards, and the to-do items they generate";
    is_m_ocl: g3 -> m_ocl "OCL, a loadable subsystem: allows editing of strings in the OCL (Object Constraint Language), adapting an external OCL editor to ArgoUML";
    to_m_persistence: CodeUnit -> m_persistence "Persistence: packages and unpackages the persistence data of the different subsystems to and from a storage medium (a flat .uml XML file or a zipped .zargo file); during save it collects each subsystem's data, during load it hands the data back to them";
    to_m_profile: CodeUnit -> m_profile "Profile (no section in the cookbook)";
    to_m_help: CodeUnit -> m_help "Help System: provides the menu actions that start the help and other documentation, and the infrastructure for context sensitive help (not yet implemented)";
    closed: CodeUnit, g0, g1, g3, m_application, m_diagrams, m_notation, m_explorer, m_codeGeneration, m_reverseEngineering, m_persistence, m_profile, m_help, m_moduleLoader, m_gui, m_model, m_internationalization, m_taskManagement, m_configuration, m_swingExtensions, m_ocl, m_critics, m_javaCodeGeneration;
}
